# Python
analysis/.ipynb_checkpoints/
# Any __pycache__, not just analysis/. One appeared under tools/ on
# 2026-10-20 and was caught in `git diff --stat` while STAGED; it never
# reached a commit, and `git log --all --diff-filter=A -- '*.pyc'` is empty.
# THE CAUSE IS KNOWN and it is the auditing of this very script: loading
# check-facts.py by file path (importlib spec_from_file_location, which is how
# its weak-anchor audit and planted-edit checks are run) imports it as a
# module and caches it. Three earlier versions of this comment were wrong --
# one invented a mechanism, one said it "reached a commit", one called the
# cause unknown on the grounds that "nothing imports check-facts.py", which
# is false precisely when you are checking it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
analysis/.venv/

.DS_Store
*.log
firmware/test/host/detector_test
firmware/test/host/display_test
firmware/test/host/replay
server/espressolog-server
espressolog-server-linux
server/internal/web/dist/*
!server/internal/web/dist/.keep
analysis/espressolog.db
analysis/espressolog.db-shm
analysis/espressolog.db-wal

